# Addresses the devvm proxy must never connect to, even for an allowlisted
# name: loopback, private, link-local (cloud metadata), CGNAT, documentation,
# multicast and reserved space. One CIDR per line; read by haproxy.cfg.
#
# host-egress.sh appends the host's own addresses to this at apply time, so a
# host with a public address is covered too. Not covered: OTHER machines on a
# LAN that uses non-private address space.
#
# IPv4 only. The proxy separately refuses every non-IPv4 answer, so there is no
# IPv6 list to keep in step.
0.0.0.0/8
10.0.0.0/8
100.64.0.0/10
127.0.0.0/8
169.254.0.0/16
172.16.0.0/12
192.0.0.0/24
192.0.2.0/24
192.31.196.0/24
192.52.193.0/24
192.88.99.0/24
192.168.0.0/16
192.175.48.0/24
198.18.0.0/15
198.51.100.0/24
203.0.113.0/24
224.0.0.0/3
